cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tallystick: an adversarial harness for accountability in delegated agentic action"
message: "If you use this corpus or harness, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koshy
    given-names: Nitin Stephen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2690-0588"
abstract: >-
  A cryptography-free adversarial scenario corpus and adjudication harness for
  studying accountability in two-party delegation disputes involving AI agents.
  850 scenarios across 34 adversarial classes and 18 adjudication baselines,
  with a derived boundary on what any evidence-determined mechanism can resolve:
  where two worlds produce identical evidence and differ in whether any account
  diverges from the record, no mechanism resolves both, and the cost can be
  denominated but not removed. Includes a documented record of six hardening declaration defects, later
  publication/reporting drifts, and the build stages written to catch those failure modes.
keywords:
  - accountability
  - delegation
  - AI agents
  - non-repudiation
  - fair exchange
  - adversarial evaluation
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-15"
version: "0.10.2"
